      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T23:01:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, agreed that the zeroing is redundant here: by the time `mfill_atomic_install_pte()` runs, `copy_from_user()` has filled all 4KB of the new folio (a short copy returns `-ENOENT` or `-EFAULT` before that), and `memcpy()` overwrites the whole reused slice from it.\n\nIt needs a second, tags-only helper, though, because `mte_zero_clear_slice_tags()` is also used by `p3s_anon_folio_zero_slice()` in aosp/4312529, where an anonymous fault does need the slice zeroed. I\u0027ve added it as a small follow-up at the end of this topic, aosp/4404637: `mte_clear_slice_tags()`, the 4KB counterpart of `mte_clear_page_tags()`, clears only the tags (`STG`/`DC GVA` rather than `STZG`/`DC GZVA`), and this path now uses it.",
      "parentUuid": "cf28ff62_a8abf97f",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "1f5ac3f00fa7dd8c1ffda11b32d6f076afe5d251",
