      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T17:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `!p3s_folio_mapped_by_slices(vma, folio)` (`folio_mapcount(folio) \u003d\u003d 1`), returning `1` here allows `move_present_ptes()` to move `src_folio` in place (updating `src_folio-\u003eindex` and `anon_vma`) without checking whether `folio` is still in the swap cache (`folio_test_swapcache(folio)` — e.g. when sibling slices in the 16KB window are still swap PTEs) or whether the physical slice offset matches `vma_slice_offset(dst_vma, dst_addr)`.\n\nThere are also four follow-up `userfaultfd` patches higher in the stack that rework or fix the code introduced here:\n- aosp/4367946 (\"ANDROID: P3S: userfaultfd: Limit compat registration to anonymous VMAs\")\n- aosp/4367974 (\"ANDROID: P3S: userfaultfd: Move swapped 16KB windows of 4KB processes\")\n- aosp/4367997 (\"ANDROID: P3S: userfaultfd: Move present 4KB slices safely\")\n- aosp/4368005 (\"ANDROID: P3S: userfaultfd: Keep the slice phase of moved swap PTEs\")\n\nCan we squash those follow-up `userfaultfd` fixes into this patch so we don\u0027t introduce `p3s_uffd_move_nr_slices()` / the `move_pages()` slice check here only to replace them up-stack?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "1f5ac3f00fa7dd8c1ffda11b32d6f076afe5d251",
