      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for looking at this closely.\n\n**Swap cache.** `move_present_ptes()` is only reached after `move_pages_ptes()` checks `PageAnonExclusive()`. It checks again under both page table locks, with the folio locked, right before calling it. A folio can\u0027t be exclusive while sibling slices still hold swap PTEs for its entry:\n- `try_to_unmap_one()` marks a swap PTE exclusive only while a single slice maps the folio, and unmapping the first slice clears `PageAnonExclusive`. When two or more slices are swapped out together, none of their swap PTEs is exclusive.\n- When one of them swaps back in, `do_swap_page()` sees a non-exclusive swap PTE. `folio_free_swap()` can\u0027t drop the swap cache while the other slices still hold the entry, so the folio is mapped without `RMAP_EXCLUSIVE`.\n\nUpstream relies on the same invariant: `do_swap_page()` has `BUG_ON(folio_test_anon(folio) \u0026\u0026 PageAnonExclusive(page))` for a swap cache folio that a swap PTE still points to. Its UFFDIO_MOVE swap cache fixes are in `move_swap_pte()`, for swap PTEs.\n\n**Slice offset.** `move_pages()` refuses a move whose source and destination start at different slices. Each range lies within one VMA, so the slices stay equal across the whole range. Each destination PTE is built with `vma_pte_add_slice(dst_vma, addr, ...)`, so it maps the physical slice that the source PTE mapped.\n\n**The follow-ups.** On the previous patchsets, the series did replace this code. Kelvin\u0027s latest upload changed that, and at the top of his series `p3s_uffd_move_nr_slices()` and the slice check are unchanged except for the errno:\n- aosp/4367946 and aosp/4367997 are no longer in the series.\n- aosp/4367974 adds a feature (moving a whole swapped-out 16KB window) rather than fixing this patch.\n- aosp/4368005 changes the slice check\u0027s errno from `-EINVAL` to `-EBUSY`. I agree with that change, since ART\u0027s `MoveIoctl()` falls back to UFFDIO_COPY on `EBUSY` but treats `EINVAL` as fatal. It\u0027s a self-contained change on top of this patch, so I\u0027d rather keep it as Kelvin\u0027s patch and have asked him to move it to the front of his series, right after this topic.\n\nSo I\u0027d prefer not to squash these, and each one is easier to review on its own.",
